.TH HSPCMP 1 "July 2026" "OpenHSP 3.8 beta1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
hspcmp \- compile Hot Soup Processor scripts
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B hspcmp
.RI [ options ]
.I file.hsp
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B hspcmp
is the HSP3 code compiler.  It converts Hot Soup Processor version 3
scripts into intermediate object files that can be executed by an HSP
runtime.
.PP
The command-line tool can compile HSP scripts, preprocess source files,
inspect keyword and source-analysis information, and execute compiled AX
object files with an HSP runtime.
.PP
The Debian package installs this command as a wrapper that supplies the OpenHSP
common include path and runtime system path by default:
.PP
.RS
.nf
--compath=/usr/lib/openhsp/common/
--syspath=/usr/lib/openhsp/
.fi
.RE
.PP
Pass a later
.B --compath
or
.B --syspath
option to use a custom tree.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-o file
Write the output object file
.RI ( .ax )
to
.IR file .
.TP
.B \-d
Generate an object file with debugging information.
.TP
.B \-p
Run preprocessing only.
.TP
.B \-c
Compile in HSP 2.55 compatible mode.
.TP
.B \-i
Read the source script as UTF-8.
.TP
.B \-u
Output string data in UTF-8.
.TP
.B \-j
Read the source script as UTF-8 and automatically select the output format.
.TP
.B \-w
Set the debug-window display flag in the object file.
.TP
.B \-s
Output a string data file
.RI ( strmap ).
.TP
.B \-m
Compile as a script for Emscripten.
.TP
.BR \-e ", " \-e0 ", " \-e1 ", " \-r ", " \-r0 ", " \-r1
Execute an object file with the runtime named in the object header.
.B \-e0
and
.B \-r0
display only the runtime name.
.B \-r
and
.B \-r1
also wait for error-code confirmation.
.TP
.BI \-h keyword
Display help for
.IR keyword .
This option is available in the Linux version.
.TP
.BI \-lk keyword
Display the HSP3 keyword list filtered by
.IR keyword .
.TP
.BI \-ll label
Analyze the source and extract the line that defines
.IR label .
.TP
.BI \-lv variable
Analyze the source and extract the line that defines
.IR variable .
.TP
.BI \-ls keyword
Analyze the source and extract the line that defines
.IR keyword .
.TP
.B \-lr
Also extract referenced lines during source analysis.
.TP
.B \-lp
Include partial keyword matches in source-analysis extraction.
.TP
.BI \-\-syspath= directory
Set the HSP system folder used when executing a runtime.
.TP
.BI \-\-compath= directory
Set the common folder searched by
.B #include
directives.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B hspcmp \-d \-oout.ax test1.hsp
Compile
.I test1.hsp
and write
.I out.ax
with debugging information.
.TP
.B hspcmp \-e test1.ax
Execute
.I test1.ax
with the HSP runtime selected by the object file.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR hsp3cl (1),
.BR hsp3dish (1),
.BR hsp3gp (1)
